From: Cinders of Chaos <noreply@cindersofchaos.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Theme: classic panels without tiled grain (seams every 99 px)

The classic theme draws every panel (palette side panel, top bar, minimap
window, dialogs' cards) with ClassicPanel: a BorderImage of panel_flat.png
(68 x 68, a 1 px bevel ring around a 66 px grain) with border 1 and the
centre in Repeat mode. At 150% scale (66 px = 99 device px) every join of
two tiles showed the dark bevel column of the image: vertical seams every
99 px over the whole palette and bar (owner screenshot, O586).

The centre is not tiled any more: the 1 px bevel stays (Stretch slices) and
the centre is a flat rectangle in the colour the grain averages (71 of 255),
times the colorize tint like UiTheme::texture does. The Windows classic
texture is flat already and keeps its stretched centre. Only the grain of
the panels is gone; no other theme uses this file.
---
 1 files changed

diff --git a/editor/qml/themes/classic/controls/ClassicPanel.qml b/editor/qml/themes/classic/controls/ClassicPanel.qml
--- a/editor/qml/themes/classic/controls/ClassicPanel.qml
+++ b/editor/qml/themes/classic/controls/ClassicPanel.qml
@@ -1,10 +1,27 @@
 import QtQuick
 import Tibia 1.0
 
+// The 1 px bevel of panel_flat.png and a plain centre (O586). The 66 px grain
+// centre used to be tiled (Repeat): at 150% scale every join of the tiles drew
+// the dark bevel column of the image as a vertical seam every 99 px.
 BorderImage {
+    id: panel
     source: Backend.uiTheme.tex + "panel_flat.png"
     smooth: false
     border { left: 1; right: 1; top: 1; bottom: 1 }
-    horizontalTileMode: BorderImage.Repeat
-    verticalTileMode: BorderImage.Repeat
+    horizontalTileMode: BorderImage.Stretch
+    verticalTileMode: BorderImage.Stretch
+
+    // Flat centre in the colour the grain averages (71 of 255), colorize tint
+    // included (UiTheme::texture multiplies the grey by the tint). The Windows
+    // classic texture is flat already: its stretched centre stays.
+    Rectangle {
+        x: 1; y: 1
+        width: Math.max(0, panel.width - 2)
+        height: Math.max(0, panel.height - 2)
+        visible: Backend.uiTheme.style === "classic"
+        color: Qt.rgba(Backend.uiTheme.tint.r * 0.279,
+                       Backend.uiTheme.tint.g * 0.279,
+                       Backend.uiTheme.tint.b * 0.279, 1)
+    }
 }
